York, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jay S. Sugarman | CEO & Chairman | Age 62 | Compensation: $677,089 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 72 people. Revenue per employee of $5.4M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $174K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Safehold Inc. New is a small-cap real estate business with a $690M market cap on $386M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +35% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 41.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 69/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 31% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (SAFE) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_SAFE_Movement_111326103602_1794584162.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Comparison: CubeSmart (NYSE:CUBE) & Safehold (NYSE:SAFE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/head-to-head-comparison-cubesmart-nysecube-safehold-nysesafe.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794583731.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"T